From 264a076dc9e9ad641ec0de34787263dae15c8d44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GNB Build <palimpseste@quidam.eu>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:42:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] companion: add dual BLE+WiFi transport, both active
 simultaneously

New env heltec_v4_companion_radio_ble_wifi / heltec_tracker_v2_companion_radio_ble_wifi
(DUAL_BLE_WIFI=1), separate from the existing companion_radio_ble/_wifi envs
(both left untouched).

Rebased onto companion-v1.17.1 (was stuck on a ~3-minor-version-old base,
the previous upstream fork we tracked has since disappeared from GitHub).
Original design (25/07) was single-transport-active, switched at reboot,
with a 30s-timeout BLE fallback if WiFi failed to join. Superseded here by
the native MultiSerialInterface introduced upstream since: Bluetooth and
WiFi are now registered as two independent interfaces and run permanently
side by side (interface_manager.loop() services both every iteration) --
no reboot switch, no "which transport is the board on" ambiguity, no
fallback logic needed since BLE never goes away in the first place.

wifi_ssid/wifi_pwd/wifi_enabled remain configurable over CMD_SET_CUSTOM_VAR
(id 41) on whichever transport is reachable -- no new protocol command
needed on the app side. No hardcoded WiFi credentials anywhere in this
build (unlike the existing plain _wifi envs, which bake WIFI_SSID/WIFI_PWD
at compile time) -- fully config-free at compile time, safe to distribute
as one binary. wifi_ssid/wifi_pwd/wifi_enabled are persisted through the
NodePrefs ConfigSerializer (CompanionPrefs::structure()), guarded by
#ifdef DUAL_BLE_WIFI so other builds are unaffected.

Not yet recompiled/retested on this base -- next step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
